{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"winded-chunky-sheldrake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe LLM gates carry leftovers from finished cutovers and one retired demo: the single-pass review-a-ticket engine (a demo the project has been retiring; the real reviews are the four-phase plan review and four-phase code review, whose single-turn criteria are steps inside those workflows), two shadow comparators, a spot-eval harness with an unreachable entry point, private re-exports that ADR 0111 forbids, severity residue from ADR 0108, a finished A/B env var, a legacy overlay routing form that clients may still use, and five attestation helpers independently confirmed dead on origin/main. Each is small; together they are the kind of retained rollback twin the operator named as the target class on 2026-09-06.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The single-pass demo is fully retired: its engine, parity harness, prompt, eval spec, and eval-solver branch are gone, the catalog has exactly one default reviewer (`code-quality`), and the four-phase plan-review and code-review workflows are byte-unchanged. Checked by the demo story's greps and the regenerate-index drift gate.\n- [ ] No finished-cutover scaffolding remains: the shadow comparators, the spot-eval harness, and the private re-exports are deleted with their only importers migrated. Checked by the scaffolding story's greps.\n- [ ] Severity no longer drives any gate policy, `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` is gone with prefetch always on, and the legacy overlay `activate:` list form warns once per overlay through the deprecation registry while still working. Checked by the priority-driven step tests, the prefetch spy test, and the two overlay warning tests.\n- [ ] The five dead attestation helpers are removed, the duplicated unresolvable-ref message is single-sourced, and the plan-review status surface emits only values its schema declares. Checked by the attestation story's greps and the parametrized status test.\n- [ ] Every client-facing change carries a release-notes line. Checked by the entries each story adds.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Cutover scaffolding story: delivers criterion 2.\n- Demo retirement story: delivers criterion 1, depends on the scaffolding story (shared test file and a relocated-prompts tuple).\n- Severity and prefetch story: delivers the severity and prefetch half of criterion 3.\n- Overlay warning story: delivers the overlay half of criterion 3, depends on the demo story for a registry note.\n- Attestation helpers story: delivers criterion 4.\n- Criterion 5 is delivered by each story's own release-notes line.","id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"LLM gates: retire the single-pass demo, finished-cutover leftovers, severity residue, and confirmed-dead attestation helpers"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788805261482281215,"uuid":"a4c7596b-f256-4143-bd4b-b0a30e4fe7e1"}